# No Legacy Re-exports

When relocating a function, type, or module to a new canonical path, move callers to the new path. Do not keep compatibility shims at the old location.

## Do not

- Re-export from the old file: `export { foo } from '$lib/new/path'`
- Leave a stub file whose only job is forwarding to the new module
- Keep the symbol in an old barrel (`index.ts`) after the move

## Do instead

1. Put the implementation in the canonical location (e.g. `$lib/utils.ts` for shared helpers).
2. Update every import to the new path.
3. Delete the old file and remove it from any barrel exports.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — legacy shim after moving debounce to $lib/utils
// src/lib/features/journal/utils/debounce.ts
export { debounce } from '$lib/utils';

// ❌ BAD — barrel still exposes moved symbol
export * from './debounce';

// ✅ GOOD — single source, direct imports
import { debounce } from '$lib/utils';
```

## When unsure

Prefer one canonical import path over multiple valid paths. If a symbol is shared across features, it belongs in `$lib/`, not under `$lib/features/<feature>/`.
